WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.050
Choosing a building involves heat, heavy rain, and years of changing needs.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.700
This is GEONOS.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:12.890
It brings maps, records, and imagery into one workspace, so we can compare two places and decide what

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.140
to check next.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.330
Select 572 and 592 Smith Street.

6
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.250
Their outlines share one scale.

7
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.610
The toolbar keeps each analysis in this comparison.

8
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.300
Native building IDs keep the selection stable as we move between tools.

9
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.050
Voice opens recording or upload.

10
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.930
Muse Voice creates an editable transcript.

11
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.050
We review it, then add it to the message.

12
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.660
Sending stays a separate action.

13
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.030
Compare asks Muse Spark for official evidence.

14
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:54.400
In the 2050 rainfall scenario, mapped water at least one foot deep touches 572.

15
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.720
The matching class is about 47 metres from 592.

16
00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.320
Next, check entrance and equipment elevations.

17
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.840
Sources identify the scenario and the returned records.

18
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.510
Climate connects station observations with regional projections.

19
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:17.350
Energy reports retain their boundaries: the same energy total produces different intensities across two

20
00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.240
reported floor areas.

21
00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.960
Units and dates travel with each figure.

22
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.530
Aerial imagery retrieves dated photographs.

23
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.730
SAM 3.1 marks roofs and trees.

24
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.260
The crosscheck compares returned roof regions with the official outline.

25
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.500
Muse Wonder turns the structured findings into survey questions.

26
00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.590
Change detection retrieves 2020 and 2024 photographs.

27
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:52.990
Run DINOv2 in the browser, inspect highlighted windows, then move the divider through the source images.

28
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.720
The model highlights visual differences in these dated images.

29
00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.900
Second review gives Muse Wonder the current public-data brief.

30
00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:09.180
Its tradeoff, assumption and decisive check help focus the next inspection.

31
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.990
Inspection visual uses Muse Image to illustrate the written checks.

32
00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:21.680
The concept helps discuss drainage, equipment and access with the project team.

33
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.910
Private notes opens the local workflow.

34
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.990
Muse Glimmer reviews a twenty-thousand-usable-square-foot requirement.

35
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.910
It requests measured plans, clear height and loading dimensions, with a conditional next step based on the

36
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.320
usable area.

37
00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.610
Export preserves the source links and follow-up checks.

38
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.810
Compare two buildings.

39
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.930
Trace the evidence.

40
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.530
Plan the next inspection.

41
00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.380
Building decisions, backed by evidence.
